# Local `act` defaults (read automatically from the repo root).
# NOTE: act only reads lines starting with "-"; inline comments after a flag
# are parsed as arguments, so keep flags on their own bare lines.
--reuse
--action-offline-mode
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
# act mounts DOCKER_HOST's socket into every job container; a colima socket is
# a macOS unix socket and cannot cross virtiofs, so the run dies in "Set up
# job". "-" disables the mount. Only the `docker` job needs a daemon inside,
# and that one is left to real CI.
--container-daemon-socket -
# Stay on the native arch: a linux/amd64 image on Apple Silicon carries an
# amd64 node, which act's post-steps cannot exec (nektos/act#107).
--env GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0
